{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30169 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Leosibirone B, (rel)- is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through a complex network of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Leosibirone B targets a sialyltransferase enzyme, which is part of a signaling pathway that ultimately influences the activity of the choline transporter. This sialyltransferase is targeted by multiple compounds, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and 5,8-Dihydroxy-2-(2-phenylethyl)chromone, which themselves are also linked to the choline transporter. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target profiles indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the sialyltransferase, which may modulate the choline transporter's function. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of sialyltransferases in mediating the effects of Leosibirone B on the choline transporter, suggesting a broader regulatory role in cellular processes.",
